{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-07-56-861Z","seq":23,"at":"2026-10-31T14:09:30.256Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C003-CH1-R0365","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Proposed go/no-go: the best-supported configuration, whichever it is, must repeatedly reproduce field crack locations and fracture features, with contrasts distinguishable from scatter and service-relevant exposure justified against approximately 18 months.","sources":[],"explanation":"“Confirmed,” “repeatedly,” field-feature matching and contrasts “distinguishable from scatter” lack acceptance rules, allowing a selected configuration to pass on loosely matched cracks or selectively interpreted replicates without establishing reproducible field failure. Add a compact prerequisite that, before held-out confirmation, the parties lock the crack-detection and field-match criteria, specimen-level replication and repeat-handling rule, treatment of ambiguous matches and runouts, contrast decision rule, and service-exposure justification.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-07-56-861Z","seq":24,"at":"2026-10-31T14:09:32.529Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},"kind":"proposal","inputs":[{"artifactId":"business-C009-CH1","version":1},{"artifactId":"scholar-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},{"artifactId":"pair-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-C009-CH1-R0288.v1.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-07-56-861Z","seq":25,"at":"2026-10-31T14:09:49.218Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-review-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1},"kind":"review","inputs":[{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-review-C001-CH1-R1008.v1.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-07-56-861Z","seq":26,"at":"2026-10-31T14:09:49.219Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Run a proposed six-week passive-replay experiment using selected site captures and separate Modbus/BACnet bench scenarios. Compare fixed-threshold rules with site-specific statistical baselines and calibrated thresholds, training and calibrating without attack examples. Select configurations on tuning data, then freeze them for independent evaluation. Proposed go/no-go targets for the best configuration, whichever wins: separately for each protocol, detect at least 90% of injected episodes within 60 seconds","sources":[{"recordId":"C001-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"What we actually need is something that learns what normal looks like on a specific site and raises a flag when behaviour drifts from that baseline.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"The proposal does not define the injected conditions, what constitutes an episode, when its 60-second clock starts, or how an alert is matched to it; an easy or heavily repeated scenario could therefore satisfy 90% without establishing meaningful anomaly coverage. Add a prerequisite to agree and freeze a per-protocol scenario inventory, episode/onset and matching rules, and scenario counts or weighting before held-out evaluation, keeping evaluation injections out of configuration selection.","owner":"proposal_writer"},{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"obtain correct explanation paraphrases from at least 80% of participating plant managers","sources":[{"recordId":"C001-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"We need a method that works with no attack examples and that we can explain to a plant manager in plain language.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"The manager denominator is stated, but neither the explanations each manager must assess nor the rule for a correct paraphrase and an overall successful manager is defined; success on one selectively easy explanation could pass without demonstrating useful comprehension. Make acceptance conditional on a pre-agreed explanation sample covering both protocols and a short scoring rubric defining per-explanation correctness and per-manager success.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-07-56-861Z","seq":27,"at":"2026-10-31T14:10:02.323Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-review-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},"kind":"review","inputs":[{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-review-C009-CH1-R0288.v1.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T14-07-56-861Z","seq":28,"at":"2026-10-31T14:10:02.325Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Report other clients and mixed-script, inflectional and unseen-product subsets separately.","sources":[{"recordId":"C009-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"We need an approach that handles lemmatisation or indexing in a way that is accurate for Serbian, tolerates script mixing automatically, and can be updated when new vocabulary arrives without a full re-index.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"},{"recordId":"C009-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"maintaining those lists manually does not scale as clients add new product terminology every quarter.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"Reporting these subsets does not prevent acceptance when mixed-script or newly introduced product queries still fail: sufficiently small subsets can fail entirely while the overall bank miss-rate confidence bound remains below 5%. Add a short prerequisite that held-out mixed-script and genuinely new-product cases must meet separately agreed useful-retrieval acceptance limits, including after the vocabulary-update rehearsal; those limits need not equal the overall 5% target.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
